{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/212","id":773760971,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz884uHqfL","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/212","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/212.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/212.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/212","number":212,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rework the CLI to use gRPC","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"First, apologise for the massive PR, I got a bit carried away. (A lot of the code is generated, and is a separate commit)\r\n\r\nThis PR moves the rest of the user facing CLI (all commands but `serve`) to use gRPC to communicate with the server.\r\n\r\nThis means that the PR has \"three layers\".\r\n\r\n1. It adds `protobuf` definitions and generate types and rpc based on this\r\n2. Then it implements the \"service\" interface provided by gRPC\r\n3. And then we move all the commands to use the new interface.\r\n4. Bonus layer: I have added integration tests for the CLI (execute command and read out result) for every command. \r\n\r\nIn between these steps, there is a lot of code cleanup and streamlining of functions to better fit the new interface. I have also made an attempt on standardising and cleaning up where we had several different ways to get information.\r\n\r\nThis means that we now have:\r\n\r\n- A CLI that communicates over rpc\r\n  - which means we can run it from everywhere when we add authentication\r\n- A Web API generated from the same spec, supporting the same as gRPC (currently disabled, due to missing auth)\r\n- Integration tests for the CLI, should help us find direct and detect underlying issues changes can cause.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat I still would like to tackle (before release):\r\nThe cli takes quite inconsistent parameters: database id, machine key, name + namespace. I think we should discuss to standardise on one main approach.","created_at":"2021-11-04T22:48:31Z","updated_at":"2022-03-02T08:56:18Z","closed_at":"2021-11-12T14:39:39Z","merged_at":"2021-11-12T14:39:39Z","merge_commit_sha":"ba650929264091f8d6dda3cf6b87ec6e7e9399a4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"juanfont","id":181059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTA1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/received_events","type":"User"